# Feature pipeline

| Attribute | Value |
|-----------|--------|
| Type | Rule |
| Audience | Parent when the user wants product work |
| Adapt | Do not add application folders or tracker URLs. Overlay those in `config.json`. |

When the user wants work done or a question about this repository, follow the
IDE `run-workflow` skill first. Run `.pipeline/loader/load_workflow.py` and
Read only `allowed_reads`.

Chains, skips, tracker settings, retry caps, and planning sign-off gates come
from `.pipeline/config.json`. File packs live in `.pipeline/workflows/`.
Feature class may run `architect-agent` after `@signoff:requirements`.

Product workflows: spawn **one new Task per agent**. `ask` stays in the parent.
Never call tracker MCP from the parent.

Hooks are optional and project-local (`.cursor/hooks.json`). If an external
agent portal already owns human-in-the-loop, pipeline hooks should yield to
that portal (see the project hook README).
